Yes, 14 Mill Wynd is in the **Glenarrow Town Centre** conservation area. It is not a listed building and has no tree preservation order.

Council guidance on windows says that replacing windows in a conservation area needs a planning application unless the new windows match the existing ones in material and pattern. So if you want to change the material (for example, from timber to uPVC) or the glazing pattern or style, you will likely need to apply. If the replacements are like-for-like, you may not need one.

I can't give a formal opinion on your specific proposal. If you're unsure whether your plans qualify, contact the planning desk before starting work. If you already have an application reference, I can look up its status for you.
